  "notes": {
    "shorter_strap_geometry_assumptions": "inputs/balloon-ttp/Shorter straps.step re-layouts the assembly with the two radiator plates stacked above/below the box (Z axis) instead of split left/right (X axis) in the original CAD, and collapses each side's connector_block+copper_strap+radiator_bracket into 1 (top path, 'strap_top') or 2 (bottom path, 'connector_bottom' -> 'strap_bottom') unlabeled solids -- a real CAD-export gap (see step_assembly SKILL.md gotcha on unlabeled parts), not a modelling choice by us. All 3 unlabeled solids are assigned bulk OFHC copper (matching the original copper_strap material) since the sub-parts cannot be geometrically distinguished as aluminum-connector vs copper-strap -- this is a conservative choice (higher conductivity than the aluminum it likely partly represents) and, per the prior transient-0-40km-etp-copper study, strap material was already shown thermally negligible next to the bolted-joint TCRs, which are carried forward unchanged (1.58 K/W per bolted joint, 0.1 K/W PTM7950 at the die)."
  }
